was founded in 1831 and is headquartered in Wayne, Pennsylvania.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Kurt J. Bitting | CEO & Director | Age 49 | Compensation: $1.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 617 people. Revenue per employee of $1.2M ranks in the top quartile among Basic Materials peers, declining at 8%/yr \u2014 weakening productivity. Each employee generates $113K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $16K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Ecovyst Inc. is a small-cap basic materials business with a $1.1B market cap on $724M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -4% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 5% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 26%.","The business throws off $70M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 10 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","Accruals are elevated at -16.8% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 1.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 4.1% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.9% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 58/100): structural revenue/margin decline; leveraged balance sheet under pressure \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Basic Materials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Commodity price volatility and cost-curve position \u2014 in a downturn only the lowest-cost producer has a business, and the rest carry the overhead.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Ecovyst Inc (ECVT) (Q3 2026) Earnings Call Highlights: Raised Guidance and Accelerating ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/ecovyst-inc-ecvt-q3-2026-111325938.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793963605.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Ecovyst (ECVT) Could Be 33% Undervalued On Raised Guidance And Buybacks","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/materials/nyse-ecvt/ecovyst/news/ecovyst-ecvt-could-be-33-undervalued-on-raised-guidance-and","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793928678.57,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.925,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance","dividend"]},{"title":"Ecovyst (ECVT) Q3 2026 